{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/417057-pandorans-other-goals-than-eat-pyros","id":417057,"title":"Pandorans: Other Goals than \"Eat Pyros?\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-23T19:09:37-08:00","id":417057,"title":"Pandorans: Other Goals than \"Eat Pyros?\"","content":"Anyway, I just remembered something I wanted to ask when I got Firestorm Fiction Anthology.<br /> <br /> In Beautiful Strange, the valravns are obvious Pandorans, but they seem a lot more intelligent than how non-Sublimati Pandorans are generally depicted, and more than that, they don't seem that interested in our Zeka protagonist, just tormenting his employers. And they've done it for a long time, to the point where they aren't familiar with Prometheans.<br /> <br /> So I was wondering, is this the new paradigm for Pandorans? They can come out of Dormancy without Azothic Radiance (by Prometheans) and there's ways to keep awake other than &quot;stay within Azothic Radiance&quot;? If so, great, I just want to know (before the vote revives someday).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:53:47-08:00","id":417100,"title":"","content":"It might be interesting to see one that wants to become human... especially if it thought it had to become a Promethean first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T06:57:00-08:00","id":417490,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the obvious Pandorans that Israel Hands and Sister Stitch witnessed when they met Windscale. They whispered to her in her sleep rather than eating her. I'm not 100% sure the valravns are Pandorans. They're tiny bit similar to Shard Crows.<br /> <br /> But yes, more diverse Pandorans are very exciting. I've always been a huge fan of the Mockeries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:21:21-08:00","id":417601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/417057-pandorans-other-goals-than-eat-pyros?p=417490#post417490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention the obvious Pandorans that Israel Hands and Sister Stitch witnessed when they met Windscale. They whispered to her in her sleep rather than eating her. I'm not 100% sure the valravns are Pandorans. <b>They're tiny bit similar to Shard Crows</b>.<br /> <br /> But yes, more diverse Pandorans are very exciting. I've always been a huge fan of the Mockeries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er...<br /> <br /> Emphasis on <i>tiny. </i>They mind control rather than possess, and I don't see them looking for soul stones to incubate, or mages. They don't even look that similar-the valravns look like normal corvids apart from their ability to speak and their seeming inability to fly, and Shard Crows look half-eaten and fly regardless.<br /> <br /> No offense intended, but I think it's a safe bet to assume they have more to do with the dominant inhuman antagonists of the native line rather than what is essentially an entry in the Monster Manual of another line. That isn't to say it's impossible, I just hope it's the more likely bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-24-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:41:48-08:00","id":417611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/417057-pandorans-other-goals-than-eat-pyros?p=417601#post417601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offense intended, but I think it's a safe bet to assume they have more to do with the dominant inhuman antagonists of the native line rather than what is essentially an entry in the Monster Manual of another line. That isn't to say it's impossible, I just hope it's the more likely bet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And likewise no offense, but considering that this book also contains clear references to weird non-Created nonsense in its other stories I don't feel terribly uncomfortable guessing that they have nothing to do with anything established. That continually remains an option in this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T10:19:14-08:00","id":417641,"title":"","content":"The Valravn is a real Myth, and they can't fly because of the sun (or radiations from the protagonist). It's clearly stated twice in the story.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I hope for better description on Pandoran goals than the simple &quot;kill-eat-rest&quot; from first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T04:25:33-08:00","id":418589,"title":"","content":"I'm personally of the opinion that the Valraven are just another creature of the World of Darkness and not Pandorans, but this is neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> It's my opinion that only the Sublimati possess the level of intelligence necessary to foster goals and purposes beyond the all consuming drive to devour Pyros. A Pandoran that awakens to a different stimuli and possesses a level of intelligence beyond that of a normal variant would seem to fall under the category of Cryptid rather than Pandoran. That's not to say that such an aberration isn't possible, just that it would be so fundamentally different from it's fellows that it should have it's own unique title and category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:43:12-08:00","id":418785,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to see some more to the Pandorans. More ways to be active, more goals, especially considering how rare Prometheans are supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Maybe it will get tied in with the alchemists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-25-2015, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}